# Trivy ignore list — vendored build-tooling CVEs, not application dependencies.
#
# These two CVEs live only inside pip's / setuptools' bundled `_vendor` build
# machinery (Trivy groups them under "Python (python-pkg)"). They are never
# imported or executed by the running SeeQL container, which runs the app
# (uvicorn / seeql) and never invokes pip or setuptools at runtime. The image's
# top-level setuptools is patched (84.x); the 70.3.0 hit is a vendored copy that
# cannot be removed without breaking pip itself.
#
# The application's own dependencies ARE patched — see constraints.txt
# (starlette, cryptography, mcp, PyJWT, pyasn1, python-multipart, msgpack, etc.).
# Re-evaluate when pip / setuptools ship updated vendored copies.
CVE-2025-47273         # setuptools path traversal — pip-vendored copy only
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964    # msgpack OOB read — pip-vendored copy only
